  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Faith acts to improve Water, sanitation and hygiene practices in Sierra Leone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The simple rationale is to reduce hygiene related disease and mortality in Sierra Leone through reinforcing CAFOD&#x2019;s current Water, Hygiene and Sanitation (WASH) programs with Malaria Consortium&#x2019;s faith based behavioural change network, resulting in greater impact of programming.
The partnership will create a more holistic, integrated program by combining the &#x201c;hardware&#x201d; of CAFOD with the &#x201c;software&#x201d; (Government approved behavioural change messaging) through partnership with Malaria Consortium&#x2019;s Faith Acts network. This combination will improve depth of impact and breadth of coverage supporting more vulnerable populations such as pregnant women and children</narrative>
  </description>
